coder › ## What changed

**`src/query.ts`** — implemented `parseQuery` and `stringifyQuery`:

- `parseQuery(text)`: strips leading `?`, splits on `&`, handles empty segments, splits on first `=`, decodes key/value with `+` → space then `decodeURIComponent`, accumulates in first-seen order (single → string, duplicate → array, further → push).
- `stringifyQuery(query)`: iterates `Object.entries` in insertion order, emits one pair per value for arrays (empty arrays → nothing), encodes with `encodeURIComponent` (space → `%20`), joins with `&`, no leading `?`.

**`src/query.test.ts`** — 24 tests covering all specified cases: empty/`?`/leading `?`/without `?`, single pair, `=` missing, repeated keys → ordered array, percent-decoding, `+` → space, value with internal `=`, stringify insertion order, array → one pair per element, empty array → nothing, space → `%20`, no leading `?`, empty object → `""`, and two round-trip tests (`parse(stringify(obj))` and `stringify(parse(x))` with encoding/arrays/spaces).

